From f3ab017a229c9eca400a55d24cd9a4f759c4baa8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephen Finucane <stephenfin@redhat.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 11:27:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] json-rpc: Rename TLS options

These options control TLS configuration for the JSON RPC server.
keystoneauth 5.17.0 adds new, identically-named options that control TLS
configuration for the *client*. Allow users to distinguish between the
two by adding a `server_` prefix to the former. Aliases are provided,
though these introduce a small upgrade impact: users who had overridden
these options to control server configuration will see the same
configuration inherited for clients (or rather, will as soon as ksa is
bumped). This will be covered via an update to the release note in a
subsequent change.

Change-Id: I1972c85de47fc70758753665488f822b4320a264
Signed-off-by: Stephen Finucane <stephenfin@redhat.com>
